    "result_text": "All green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner response for the OfficeFloor `POST /api/owners` (create) and `GET /api/owners/{id}` (read) endpoints. It returns `true` when **any** of the three conditions hold, else `false`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` boolean to the `OwnerDto` schema (so the generated DTO gets `getRiskFlag`/`setRiskFlag`), documenting the three trigger conditions.\n\n2. **`DisposableDomains.java`** (new) \u2014 shared source of truth for the disposable-domain blocklist (moved out of `OwnerEmail`) plus `isAdjacent(email)`, which recognises *disposable-adjacent* domains: a subdomain of a blocked domain (`inbox.mailinator.com`) or one sharing a blocked domain's second-level label under a different TLD (`tempmail.io`). Exact blocked domains are already rejected with 400 upstream, so this softer check is what a persisted owner can actually trip.\n\n3. **`RiskFlag.java`** (new) \u2014 computes the flag: `possibleDuplicate` true **OR** disposable-adjacent email **OR** city over its soft capacity (\u2265 40 owners, the same threshold at which `CapacityWarning` begins, counted case-insensitively to match `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`).\n\n4. **`OwnerEmail.java`** \u2014 refactored to reference `DisposableDomains.BLOCKED` (no behavior change).\n\n5. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** / **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 set `dto.setRiskFlag(RiskFlag.riskFor(owner, ownerRepository))` at response time, alongside the existing `capacityWarning`/`bulkSignupWarning` enrichment.\n\nThe visible test `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` (a unique, email-less owner in a fresh city \u2192 `riskFlag: false`) passes, and the full suite builds green.\n\nA note on the two spots where the spec left room to interpret, in case you want to steer them: I read *\"disposable-adjacent\"* as subdomain/second-level-label resemblance to the existing blocklist, and *\"over its soft capacity\"* as the city holding \u2265 40 owners (the established warning threshold, hard limit being 50). Both are documented in the OpenAPI description. Happy to tighten either definition if the intended rule differs.",
